+## Lifecycle
+
+Executor serves the shared `robonix/lifecycle/driver` on its gRPC endpoint.
+After the endpoint is callable, startup invokes INIT and ACTIVATE through that
+Driver, publishing REGISTERED → INACTIVE → ACTIVE. Startup errors terminate
+the process. Execute accepts new plans only after activation; health, status,
+plan cancellation, and Driver remain callable while inactive.
+
+DEACTIVATE and SHUTDOWN close admission before cancelling all active plans.
+Unstarted nodes are skipped, asynchronous capabilities receive their cancel
+request, and synchronous calls already running may return naturally. Descendant
+tasks and verification finish before the final plan event is queued and the
+plan leaves the active table. Drain has a five-second budget. If work or cleanup
+does not finish, Driver returns `ok=false`, keeps admission closed, and does not
+publish INACTIVE or TERMINATED. Retry after completing or cancelling the work.
+ACTIVATE cannot reopen admission while a failed drain still owns work.
+
+SHUTDOWN publishes TERMINATED only after cleanup, stops heartbeat and the gRPC
+server, and exits the process. Server shutdown has a five-second grace period;
+exceeding it produces an error exit. Repeated commands for the same valid state
+are safe. INIT in ACTIVE and activation before INIT are rejected without
+cancelling existing plans. Duplicate active plan ids are rejected.
+
